<title>USA: TABLE - Isomedix Inc Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Isomedix Inc Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>WHIPPANY, N.J. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended   Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				  June 30,		June 30,</p>
<p>			   1997	 1996	  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Sales	  $13,598,253 $11,562,127 $25,588,093 $22,354,859</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>		    3,876,158   3,051,337   6,706,913   5,473,893</p>
<p>Income from continuing</p>
<p>  operations    2,296,958   1,892,799   4,037,327   3,388,179</p>
<p>Discontinued</p>
<p>  operations	200,150  ( 118,084)     200,150  ( 128,963)</p>
<p> Net income     2,497,108   1,774,715   4,237,477   3,259,216</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>		    6,653,493   7,172,600   6,676,640   7,182,112</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share:</p>
<p>Continuing operations</p>
<p>			    .35	   .26	   .60	   .47</p>
<p>Discontinued operations</p>
<p>			    .03	 (.01)	   .03	 (.02)</p>
<p> Net income	     .38	   .25	   .63	   .45</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said its increased sales for Q2 reflect results from its Vega Alta, Puerto Rico location, acquired in March 1997.</p>
<p>The company said its increase in income from discontinued operations for Q2 1997 reflect the sale of fixed assets from its discontinued Skyland operation in June 1997.</p>
